{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1518776-looking-for-an-adventure","id":1518776,"title":"Looking for an adventure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-25T14:16:08-07:00","id":1518776,"title":"Looking for an adventure","content":"All,<br /> I am going to run my first Lunars 3E game and am looking for a pre-made adventure since I don't have much free time to prepare. I couldn't find anything on the ST vault so I'm hoping y'all might be able to point me to something. Thank you in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T18:13:45-07:00","id":1518797,"title":"","content":"There aren't a lot of published adventures for Exalted. For 3E, the only one I know off the top of my head is the Tomb of Dreams quickstart. How familiar are you with the setting? How familiar are you with prior editions? There are a small number of modules for 1E and 2E, but you'd need to convert stat blocks, and the setting info is a little different in 3E. There was the Tomb of 5 Corners and Time of Tumult in 1E, and the Return to the Tomb of 5 Corners, Contagion of Law, and Daughter of Nexus in 2E. I might be missing a couple, but there aren't a lot of them. And your mileage may vary, but I didn't find most of them to be top tier - they're okay, but not great. <br /> <br /> I've had more luck taking published adventures from other systems and using them as inspiration. For example, I'm currently running the Reavers of Harkenwold, a D&amp;D 4e module, using the Nentir Vale setting as the inspiration for one of the Hundred Kingdoms in the River Province. The basic plot is very compatible with Exalted - a group of mercenaries has taken over a territory, and the PCs get involved with the local resistance. Make the leader of the mercenaries a DB with several DB or god-blooded lieutenants, ignore the references to dwarves, elves, etc. and just make them humans, replace references to D&amp;D gods with Exalted's celestial gods or make your own local terrestrial gods, etc. The nest of goblins can become Fair Folk hobgoblins, and the necromancer's keep became a manse under the control of a powerful pre-Contagion ghost in a small shadowland. If you are pretty comfortable with Creation as a setting, this is pretty easy. If you're new to Exalted, though, then it might not be much of a time saver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T18:33:27-07:00","id":1519062,"title":"","content":"I thought that there was a free adventure somewhere on here for Exalted 3E by Ekorren, but I can't find it now as it looks like they nuked their homebrew hub. I seem to recall it being better looking than any of the paid stuff that was released back in the WW days, though I haven't run it myself. Not sure how well it would work for Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}